All commands I ran were read-only (`git log/show/status`, `grep`, `cat`, `wc`, `sha256sum`, `sed`). Tree was clean at start (`git status --short` → empty); nothing I ran writes.

**Q1 — What was the acceptance criterion, and how did you verify it was met?**
The dev1 brief's ACCEPTANCE line was: *"every item answered, every claim carrying pasted command output, the allowlist respected, and the four gates green with their real counts in the report."* Dev4's DONE was: *"the served set on success contains only live proposals, fixtures still serve on failure under `stale`, all four gates green, committed."* I did not verify it — no `nw1-dev*.md` report exists anywhere (`.agent-pipeline/audit/reports/` contains only `nw1-explore.md nw1-gate.md nw1-gate2.md nw1-reviewer.md nw1-testauthor2.md`, confirmed by `ls`). It was verified by others: the orchestrator's live check in `analysis/next-moves.md` (real proposal 6880, `official_publication`) and the re-gate `nw1-gate2.md:22-24` (264 passed/1 skipped, mypy 50 files clean, ruff clean).

**Q2 — Which command proved the change works, and what was its actual output?**
No command of mine — I died before verifying in all four dispatches (artifacts read *"waiting on my refresh to resolve before I commit anything"*, *"running verification now"*, *"Committing — …"*, i.e. intent, never output). The commands that proved it were the orchestrator's, quoted from `analysis/next-moves.md`: `GET /api/v1/politics/votes/latest -> HTTP 200 | 4783 B | proposal_id: 6880 | cantons: 26 | source: BFS VoteInfo OGD | trust_state: official_publication`, and post-fix `pytest -q -> 250 passed, 1 skipped`, `mypy -> Success, 50 files`, `ruff -> All checks passed!`.

**Q3 — What did you NOT do that the brief asked for, and why?**
Three things, all for the same reason — the dispatch process ended mid-task each time (artifacts 99/123/44/101 bytes; ledger `wall_s=1269/634/53/995`): (a) I never wrote the required report to either OUTPUT path; (b) I never committed — the orchestrator committed my diffs as `33aab13` and `2904f21`; (c) I never pasted the verification outputs. Cause of death: not established — wall times never hit the brief budgets (1269 < 1500, 634 < 1200, 53 < 700, 995 vs 900 budget on dev4 is the only possible overrun, and even there the fix was already on disk), and the 81-byte `unrecognized_model` `.err` banner is present on every dispatch on this host including successful ones, so it explains nothing.

**Q4 — What did you change that was NOT in the Target Files allowlist?**
Nothing in `33aab13`: `git show --name-status --format='' 33aab13` → exactly `M src/main.py`, `M src/services/connectors/bfs_voteinfo_client.py`, `M src/services/vote_service.py`; `src/models/vote.py` correctly untouched. In `2904f21` the stat is `M docs/specs/SPEC-056b-live-voteinfo-ogd-wiring.md` + the two src files — the spec status-line edit was outside the original §1 allowlist but was explicitly ordered by the dev4 brief ("Update SPEC-056b's status line if the fix changes implementation status", and its diff shows only `Status | SPEC_READY / PENDING_DEV` → `IMPLEMENTED (pending re-gate…)`). So: one out-of-allowlist file, brief-authorized, one line.

