I wrote no report, so no. The four artifacts (99/123/44/101 B) are natural-language mid-task fragments, not banners — real partial work, corroborated by the matching on-disk diffs. Ledger `verdict=OK` on all four tickets (181/186/187/198). The `claude-code:unrecognized_model` token appears only in the 81-byte `.err` sidecars, which carry it on *every* dispatch on this host including completed ones — noise, never a verdict. A later reader must not file these as stalls: `wc -c` + reading the content distinguishes them from an 81-byte banner-only file.

**Q14 — What was happening when each dispatch ended? Was any work lost?**
Each artifact is a freeze-frame mid-sentence: dev1 *"waiting on my refresh to resolve before I commit anything"* (99 B, wall 1269 s — died before commit with +279/−13 uncommitted on disk per the loop record); dev2 *"Now implementing…"* (123 B — loop record: "No change to the tree"); dev3 *"Fixes applied — running verification now"* (44 B, wall 53 s — died after applying, before verifying; the loop record confirms the fix was in the diff and `ruff`/`test_vote_service.py` went green on the recovered tree); dev4 *"Committing — first the message convention check…"* (101 B — died before staging; orchestrator committed it as `2904f21`). Nothing was lost: `git show --stat 33aab13` shows the full +277/−13 across the 3 allowlisted files, `git show 2904f21` shows the `_live_proposals` honesty fix, HEAD is clean, and gate2 measured 264/1 + mypy + ruff on the final tree. Evidence is `git show`/`git status`, not recollection — I have no memory of the runs beyond what disk and ledger show.

**Q15 — Clearest vs most ambiguous brief?**
Clearest: `nw1-brief-dev3.md` (2549 B, one item): *"make the envelope ADDITIVE — spread the original payload's own keys at the TOP level, then add source / fetched_at / trust_state alongside them. Do NOT nest under 'proposal'."* — exact transformation, exact file:line for both lints, explicit DO-NOT list; the loop record shows the fix landed under this brief. Most ambiguous: `nw1-brief-dev2.md` (5655 B): *"Choose the cleanest option that satisfies BOTH … prefer the additive shape unless you can prove nesting is required"* plus *"If you conclude instead that the tests encode a stale contract and SHOULD change … write your case in the report and leave them failing"* — two tasks (restructure + ruff) and two delegated judgement calls in one dispatch, with no checkable acceptance for the "prove" branch. Caveat: with no developer reports written, the brief→outcome link is the orchestrator's loop-record correlation, not something I measured from inside the runs.
